<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on the final day of</p>
<p>four-day English County Championship cricket matches on</p>
<p>Saturday:</p>
<p>At Southampton: Leicestershire beat Hampshire by 5 wickets.</p>
<p>Hampshire 285 and 182 (A.Pierson 4-58). Leicestershire 349 and</p>
<p>119-5. Leicestershire 23 points, Hampshire 6..</p>
<p>At Canterbury: Glamorgan beat Kent by 87 runs. Glamorgan 279</p>
<p>and 193 (S.James 54; M.Fleming 4-28, P.Strang 4-59). Kent 154</p>
<p>and 231 (A.Wells 84; D.Cosker 4-64). Glamorgan 22 points, Kent</p>
<p>4.</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Nottinghamshire beat Lancashire by 6</p>
<p>wickets. Lancashire 125 and 357 (J.Crawley 101, M.Atherton 68,</p>
<p>G.Lloyd 62). Nottinghamshire 263 and 223-4 (P.Johnson 87 not</p>
<p>out, U.Afzaal 77 not out). Nottinghamshire 22 points, Lancashire</p>
<p>6.</p>
<p>At Taunton: Match abandoned as a draw - rain. Sussex 241 and</p>
<p>259-5 (W.Athey 138 not out). Somerset 409 (G.Rose 191, R.Harden</p>
<p>103; P.Jarvis 5-122). Somerset 11 points, Sussex 8.</p>
<p>At Chelmsford: Essex beat Durham by 125 runs. Essex 237 and</p>
<p>366-9 declared (S.Law 118 not out, P.Prichard 80, N.Hussain 67;</p>
<p>M.Foster 4-94). Durham 291 and.187 (J.Morris 76; P.Such 6-55).</p>
<p>Essex 21 points, Durham 6.</p>
</text>
